                <pb facs="0730" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1946v04/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.P.(Gen)Doc.1.J.34.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article 32</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-outside-research" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1946-10-15T23:59:59+01:00" notBefore="1946-07-29T00:00:00+01:00"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>After Article 32 add a new article 32 bis reading as follows: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Bulgaria undertakes to cede within three
                                months from the date of entry into force of the present Treaty a
                                free zone on the Danube</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Port of
                                Lom</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">equipped at her own expense for
                                transit trade</hi>.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">A special commission of experts composed of
                                representatives of Greece, Bulgaria, Hungary and Roumania, convened
                                within the month following the entry into force of the present
                                Treaty, under the chairmanship of a neutral member, chosen by the
                                Economic Commission of the United Nations, will proceed to draw up
                                the main technical, economic and administrative clauses governing
                                the operation under conditions of complete equality of the Free Zone
                                and of its port and railroad facilities</hi>.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Any dispute concerning the interpretation of
                                the above paragraphs will be referred, on the request of the
                                interested party, to an arbitrator designated by the Economic
                                Commission of the United Nations whose ruling will be
                            final</hi>.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
